{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he made.</b> The two great ones are called [so] relative to the other stars, just as the three sons of Jesse are called \"the great ones\" relative to the others, and Eliab the firstborn was greater than all of them—and not [a case of] one greater than the other. There is a sod." "<b>To rule the day.</b> The sun's rule is by day and not by night, for it has no light [then]; likewise the moon and stars—their light is not seen by day. And if one asks: have not the scholars of the spheres said that the star of Zedek [Jupiter] and all the stars except the star of Nogah [Venus] are greater than the moon—so how is \"the great ones\" written? The answer: the meaning of \"the great ones\" is not their measure in their bodies but rather their light, and the moon's light is double and doubled because it is close to the earth, as it is written: מאור."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:39.114728823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}